    "grid_threshold_on_out_of_fold": 0.22,
    "rationale": "Consumer is an offensive analyst deciding whether to keep extra protection in. A missed blitz gives up a free rusher; a false alarm costs one route runner. 3:1 is an ASSUMPTION, not a measurement -- see cost_ratio_sensitivity for how the operating point moves.",
    "cost_ratio_provenance": "Asserted, not measured. analyze_cost_ratio.py attempts to derive it from EPA and fails to identify it (pff_role is post-snap, so 'extra blocker' marks max-protect play design rather than a protection call; the false-alarm cost comes out wrong-signed). That analysis does show a sack costs ~2.06 EPA and a blitz adds 2.7pp of sack risk, but the net EPA effect of a blitz is only ~-0.036 (95% CI -0.094 to +0.025), which bounds what any blitz warning can be worth. See models/cost_ratio_analysis.json.",
